      "description": "Watch Vitoria vs Bahia highlights and goals from Brasileirão on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 23, 2026. The heat of the Brazilian rivalry took center stage on August 23, 2026, as Vitória hosted Bahia in a highly anticipated Serie A encounter. Both teams stepped onto the pitch knowing that more than just three points were at stake in this tactical battle of attrition. A Gritty Opening Half The first 45 minutes were defined by physical duels and defensive discipline rather than fluid attacking play. Vitória attempted to use their home advantage to pressure the visitors, but the game remained deadlocked in midfield. The tension boiled over in the 26th minute when Matheuzinho was cautioned for a heavy challenge. Bahia responded with tactical fouls of their own, leading to a yellow card for Rodrigo Nestor just before the break. As the referee blew for halftime, both managers clearly had plenty of tactical adjustments to discuss after a scoreless opening period. Tactical Shifts Lead to the Breakthrough The second half saw immediate changes, with Bahia introducing Tomas Pochettino and Emmanuel Martinez to inject creativity. The momentum shifted decisively in the 67th minute when Erick Pulga found space to deliver a clinical assist to Alejo Veliz , who finished expertly to give the visitors the lead. Vitória responded by throwing on Renato Kayzer in an attempt to salvage a point, but they struggled to break down a resolute defensive line. Even as the game grew more desperate and Erick Pulga received a yellow card, the visitors remained composed under pressure. Late Drama Seals the Result As the match entered seven minutes of stoppage time, the home side pushed forward, leaving gaps in their defense. In the 97th minute, Bahia exploited those spaces perfectly. Michel Araujo played a pinpoint pass to Jean Lucas , who stayed calm to slot the ball home and double the lead. The late goal sparked emotional scenes, resulting in yellow cards for both Jean Lucas and Vitória's Caca . The final whistle moments later confirmed a vital away victory for Bahia , leaving the home crowd disappointed as the visitors celebrated a clinical performance."
